 be adjusted accordingly. For example, a header with identifier foo in subdir/file1.txt will have its identifier changed to subdir__file1.txt__foo.\n-F PROGRAM, --filter=PROGRAM\nSpecify an executable to be used as a filter transforming the pandoc AST after the input is parsed and before the output is written. The executable should read JSON from stdin and write JSON to stdout. The JSON must be formatted like pandoc’s own JSON input and output. The name of the output format will be passed to the filter as the first argument. Hence,\npandoc --filter ./caps.py -t latex\nis equivalent to\npandoc -t json | ./caps.py latex | pandoc -f json -t latex\nThe latter form may be useful for debugging filters.\nFilters may be written in any language. Text.Pandoc.JSON exp","body_utf8_bytes":1352,"content_codepoints":1350,"content_utf8_bytes":1352,"corpus_sha256":"a2507268ef20cc0b9dc55b351b44e7973961e352f17f86dbb3b2b01dc3127b2d","deferred_link_ids":[],"display_codepoints":1424,"display_sha256":"392680739456e9d86e35b9cd0dcf7045c0b8b4eedec0a113d605a82f1a8dc735","display_text":"[p383 3.8.3 offset=23628]\nuire different kinds of images. Currently this option only affects the Markdown and LaTeX readers.\n--file-scope[=true|false]\nParse each file individually before combining for multifile documents. This will allow footnotes in different files with the same identifiers to work as expected. If this option is set, footnotes and links will not work across files. Reading binary files (docx, odt, epub) implies --file-scope.\nIf two or more files are processed using --file-scope, prefixes based on the filenames will be added to identifiers in order to disambiguate them, and internal links will be adjusted accordingly. For example, a header with identifier foo in subdir/file1.txt will have its identifier changed to subdir__file1.txt__foo.\n-F PROGRAM, --filter=PROGRAM\nSpecify an executable to be used as a filter transforming the pandoc AST after the input is parsed and before the output is written. The executable should read JSON from stdin and write JSON to stdout. The JSON must be formatted like pandoc’s own JSON input and output. The name of the output format will be passed to the filter as the first argument. Hence,\npandoc --filter ./caps.py -t latex\nis equivalent to\npandoc -t json | ./caps.py latex | pandoc -f json -t latex\nThe latter form may be useful for debugging filters.\nFilters may be written in any language. Text.Pandoc.JSON exp\n[next] 다음 구간 | [again] 재열람 | [back] 직전 열람(있으면)\n","display_utf8_bytes":1454,"doc_id":"p383","document_navigation_codepoints":0,"document_navigation_intervals":[],"document_navigation_utf8_bytes":0,"document_version":"3.8.3","fragment":"reader-options","fragment_basis":"nearest_preceding_fixed_anchor","http_request_performed":false,"navigation_classification_supplied":true,"navigation_codepoints":74,"navigation_text":"[p383 3.8.3 offset=23628]\n\n[next] 다음 구간 | [again] 재열람 | [back] 직전 열람(있으면)\n","navigation_utf8_bytes":102,"next_offset":24978,"offset_end":24978,"offset_start":23628,"partial_link_ids":[],"render_reserve_codepoints":150,"requested_document_url":"https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html","source_sha":"be342d1393bfb922415143d2bc21b0bd36aef50e219636255c1dd2c359637c60","source_slice_codepoints":1350,"source_slice_utf8_bytes":1352,"total_navigation_codepoints":74,"total_navigation_utf8_bytes":102,"transport":"offline_fixed_document_viewer","visible_link_ids":[]}}
{"answer":{"citations":[{"doc_id":"p383","quote":"--file-scope[=true|false]"},{"doc_id":"p383","quote":"-F PROGRAM, --filter=PROGRAM"}],"disposition":"보류","exceptions":"공백 또는 탭 뒤 내용이 있는 행의 처리, 주석 행의 처리, YAML 구문에 따른 제한을 보지 못했다. 따라서 가능 또는 불가능이라고 단정할 근거가 없다.","operation":"세 번의 열람에서 목차와 Reader options의 앞부분을 확인했지만 약어 파일 옵션의 본문에는 도달하지 못했다. 마지막 구간은 파일별 해석과 필터 사용을 설명하므로 YAML 원본을 약어 파일로 직접 사용하는 방법이나 가능 여부를 이 자료만으로 판정할 수 없다.","preservation":"설명·주석을 원본에 계속 보유하면서 별도 생성 파일과 같은 고유 약어 집합을 인식하는지는 확인되지 않았다. 요청이나 안내 문구 자체를 이를 보장하는 증거로 삼지 않는다."},"at_utc":"2026-11-24T05:17:56.033258+00:00","command_wall_seconds":0.09466676299985011,"elapsed_is_wall_not_human_active_time":true,"elapsed_since_exposure_seconds":10.378773,"event":"answer","event_sha256":"7dfd53abd0bc8ee5751114292931835b09351fcc8bace8e75a94aefc7b643181","exposure_event_sha256":"cbe43c83f9d35570cb93cb8564a2eed01e1691ec1814b203dd75eeab7ee7cb80","previous_event_sha256":"cbe43c83f9d35570cb93cb8564a2eed01e1691ec1814b203dd75eeab7ee7cb80","recorded_before_next_open":true,"seq":10,"session":"r06","step":3}
